    "final_answer": "I have all the information needed. Let me provide the final answer based on the Hugging Face PEFT documentation.\n\n## Answer: Loading Adapters with PEFT in 8-bit or 4-bit\n\nI found the relevant tutorial in the **Quantization** section of the Hugging Face PEFT documentation at:\n`https://huggingface.co/docs/peft/developer_guides/quantization`\n\nThe tutorial explains that **bitsandbytes** is a quantization library with a Transformers integration that lets you quantize a model to 8 or 4-bits and enable many other options by configuring the `BitsAndBytesConfig` class.\n\n### Key Options for `BitsAndBytesConfig`:\n- Set `load_in_4bit=True` to quantize the model to 4-bits when you load it\n- Set `bnb_4bit_quant_type=\"nf4\"` to use a special 4-bit data type for weights initialized from a normal distribution\n- Set `bnb_4bit_use_double_quant=True` to use a nested quantization scheme to quantize the already quantized weights\n- Set `bnb_4bit_compute_dtype=torch.bfloat16` to use bfloat16 for faster computation\n\n### Code Example (4-bit / QLoRA-style):\n\n```python\nimport torch\nfrom transformers import BitsAndBytesConfig\n\nconfig = BitsAndBytesConfig(\n    load_in_4bit=True,                # use load_in_8bit=True for 8-bit\n    bnb_4bit_quant_type=\"nf4\",\n    bnb_4bit_use_double_quant=True,\n    bnb_4bit_compute_dtype=torch.bfloat16,\n)\n```\n\nThen pass the `config` to the `from_pretrained()` method:\n```python\nfrom transformers import AutoModelForCausalLM\nmodel = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n    \"mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1\",\n    quantization_config=config,\n)\n```\n\nNext, preprocess the quantized model for training:\n```python\nfrom peft import prepare_model_for_kbit_training\nmodel = prepare_model_for_kbit_training(model)\n```\n\nCreate a `LoraConfig`:\n```python\nfrom peft import LoraConfig\nconfig = LoraConfig(\n    r=16,\n    lora_alpha=8,\n    target_modules=[\"q_proj\", \"k_proj\", \"v_proj\", \"o_proj\"],\n    lora_dropout=0.05,\n    bias=\"none\",\n    task_type=\"CAUSAL_LM\",\n)\n```\n\nThen wrap the model with `get_peft_model()` to attach the PEFT adapter:\n```python\nfrom peft import get_peft_model\nmodel = get_peft_model(model, config)\n```\n\n### Summary for 8-bit vs 4-bit:\n- **For 4-bit (QLoRA)**: use `load_in_4bit=True` in `BitsAndBytesConfig`\n- **For 8-bit**: use `load_in_8bit=True` in `BitsAndBytesConfig`\n\nBoth follow the same workflow — configure `BitsAndBytesConfig`, pass it to `from_pretrained`, call `prepare_model_for_kbit_training()`, then wrap with a PEFT adapter via `get_peft_model()`.",
